# The reverse-engineering archive of the old beta (com.alex.recorder.beta).
# The analysis itself is tracked; the bulk - the pulled APK, the decompiled
# third-party library sources and the native .so files - is not. It is
# regenerable from the APK and would add ~230 MB of noise to the repository.
analysis/legacy-com.alex.recorder.beta/bulk/

# Build outputs
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex
*.hprof

# Build logs
*.log

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Release signing - never commit these.
#
# Android identifies an app by its signing key: if these files end up in the
# repository they can be used to sign a fake update of this app. Keep a
# private backup outside the project instead, because without them you can
# never publish an update over an already installed release.
keystore/
keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
